          "id": "q1",
          "question": "Define an Operating System. Explain its main objectives and functions. How does it act as a Resource Manager?",
          "answer": "1. Definition\n An Operating System (OS) is system software that acts as an interface between the user and computer\n hardware. It manages computer resources such as the CPU, memory, files and input/output devices.\n\n Examples: Windows, Linux, macOS and Android.\n\n 2. Main objectives of an Operating System\n  1. Convenience: Makes the computer easy to use.\n\n  2. Efficiency: Uses hardware resources efficiently.\n\n  3. Resource management: Allocates CPU time, memory and devices to programs.\n\n  4. Security: Protects data and prevents unauthorized access.\n\n  5. Error handling: Detects and handles errors during program execution.\n\n 3. Functions of an Operating System\n  • Process management: Creates and terminates processes, allocates CPU time and handles scheduling.\n\n  • Memory management: Tracks memory usage, allocates and frees memory, and supports virtual\n    memory.\n\n  • File management: Creates, deletes, stores and organizes files and controls file permissions.\n\n  • Device management: Manages devices such as printers, keyboards and disks using device drivers.\n\n  • Security and protection: Provides authentication, permissions and protection against unauthorized\n    access.\n\n  • User interface: Allows users to interact through a Command Line Interface (CLI) or Graphical User\n    Interface (GUI).\n\n  • Error detection: Detects hardware and software errors and takes suitable action.\n\n 4. Operating System as a Resource Manager\n A computer has limited resources such as CPU, RAM, storage and input/output devices. The OS\n manages these resources and distributes them among different programs.\n\n  • If two programs need the CPU, the OS decides which program gets CPU time first.\n\n  • If multiple programs need RAM, the OS allocates memory to each program.\n\n  • If two programs want to use a printer, the OS manages access to the printer.\n\n                                     USERS / APPLICATION PROGRAMS\n\n                                                        ↓\n\n                     OPERATING SYSTEM – Resource allocation and management\n\n                                                        ↓\n\n                          CPU | MAIN MEMORY (RAM) | STORAGE | I/O DEVICES\n\n\n Conclusion: An Operating System acts as a bridge between users and hardware and manages\n computer resources efficiently."
